  "id": "COMPOUND:30122 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "Paeonidaninol A is implicated in the targeting of multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the Inner centromere protein. The evidence suggests that Paeonidaninol A acts as a target for Pseudomonalisin, which in turn is targeted by Tesetaxel, and both of these compounds are targeted by the Inner centromere protein. This indicates a potential hierarchical relationship where Paeonidaninol A may influence the activity of Pseudomonalisin, which then interacts with Tesetaxel, both of which are linked to the Inner centromere protein. The presence of multiple indirect pathways supports the idea that Paeonidaninol A may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on the Inner centromere protein. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network involved, suggesting that Paeonidaninol A may play a role in modulating the activity of these downstream targets.",
